\ A legal equal-choice width is always a positive integer.
\ Invalid option counts must never reach decimal division by zero.
\ The public, narrow and wide entrypoints all fail closed by placing
\ zero in the selected quantity (zero is never a valid option index).

The invalidoptions is a wide quantity.

To check zero option count refusal:
  Put "1" into the seal inquiry's current answer.
  Put "100" into the seal inquiry's selected quantity.
  Put "0" into the invalidoptions.
  Determine canonical equal selection given the invalidoptions.
  If the seal inquiry's selected quantity is not "0",
    put "The public chooser accepted zero options." into the check report; exit.
  Put "100" into the seal inquiry's selected quantity.
  Choose narrow quantity values from the invalidoptions.
  If the seal inquiry's selected quantity is not "0",
    put "The narrow chooser accepted zero options." into the check report; exit.
  Put "100" into the seal inquiry's selected quantity.
  Perform wide option selection given the invalidoptions.
  If the seal inquiry's selected quantity is not "0",
    put "The wide chooser accepted zero options." into the check report; exit.
  Put "" into the invalidoptions.
  Determine canonical equal selection given the invalidoptions.
  If the seal inquiry's selected quantity is not "0",
    put "The public chooser accepted a blank option count." into the check report; exit.
  Put "1" into the invalidoptions.
  Determine canonical equal selection given the invalidoptions.
  If the seal inquiry's selected quantity is not "1",
    put "Rejecting zero poisoned a later valid choice." into the check report; exit.
